## Context

The author selected `untrusted-runner` for the dedicated Unix identity used at
the target boundary. Normally it runs only the external target process. R10's
egress arm places its tracer, isolation mechanism and inner target-driving
`run.py --drive` process under the same identity because the switch must enclose
that stack; the outer driver and artifact writer remain the operator's. The old
name `tester` was ambiguous enough to make the whole repository suite look as
though it should run under that account. `DECISIONS.md` records the ruling first.

This is a naming migration, not a security-model change. Historical decisions,
ticket logs and measurement artifacts remain verbatim.

## Actions

- Change the single default account constant and every live provisioning or
  diagnostic reference to `untrusted-runner`.
- Make current tests use the new name when testing the default role.
- State explicitly that the operator runs `make check`, pytest, the outer
  harness and artifact writer; name R10's inner-driver/tracer exception.
- Give separate fresh-host and UID-preserving existing-account procedures, then
  re-verify ACLs and sudoers; the harness never creates or renames accounts.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] No live code or fresh-host instruction calls the account `tester`; the
      UID-preserving migration names it only as the source identity.
- [ ] Historical records remain unchanged.
- [ ] Identity inheritance, refusal and isolation-order controls pass under the
      new name.
- [ ] `make check` and `./tickets/erg check tickets/` pass.
